StrideWear Documentation Analysis
Project Overview
StrideWear is a full-stack sportswear e-commerce web application using TanStack (Start/Router/Query/Table) on the frontend and Supabase (Postgres, Auth, Storage, Edge Functions) on the backend, with Cash on Delivery (COD) as the payment method.
Document-by-Document Analysis
01-SRS.md (Software Requirements Specification)
Status: Well-structured, comprehensive
- 8 functional requirement groups: Auth, Product Catalog, Cart/Checkout, Orders, Reviews, Wishlist, Admin Dashboard, Notifications
- Non-functional requirements: Performance (<2s load), Scalability (10K+ SKUs), Security (RLS), Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA), SEO (SSR)
- User roles: Guest, Customer, Admin, Super Admin (optional)
- Key features: Variant support (size × color), promo codes, COD checkout, order tracking, wishlist, reviews
- Gap: No mention of refund/return policy details beyond "refunded" status
02-HLD.md (High-Level Design)
Status: Clear architecture
- Architecture: Browser → TanStack Start (SSR) → Supabase → Third-party (Resend)
- 5 modules: Storefront, Cart/Checkout, Account, Admin, Notifications
- Security model: Anon key client-side, service-role server-side only, RLS everywhere
- Checkout flow: Cart → Checkout Page → COD Order Creation → Order Confirmation
- Non-goals (v1): Multi-currency, native mobile, marketplace
03-LLD-Database-Schema.md
Status: Thorough schema design
- 13 tables: profiles, addresses, categories, products, product_variants, product_images, cart_items, coupons, orders, order_items, order_status_history, reviews, wishlist_items
- Key design decisions:
- Variant-based inventory (size × color with independent stock)
- Denormalized avg_rating on products (trigger-updated)
- JSONB shipping_address snapshot on orders
- order_status_history for audit trail
- RLS: Default-deny, explicit policies per table
- Indexes: Category, status, gender, full-text search on products
04-API-Documentation.md
Status: Clear API contract
- 2 Edge Functions:
1. POST /send-order-email - Transactional emails
2. POST /admin/update-order-status - Admin order management
- Direct Supabase access: Products, Cart, Wishlist, Orders, Reviews via typed hooks
- Query key conventions: Well-defined for cache invalidation
05-Test-Plan.md
Status: Solid foundation
- 5 test types: Unit (Vitest), Component, Integration, E2E (Playwright), Manual
- 15 sample test cases covering auth, filtering, cart, checkout, RLS, admin, performance
- Key security test: TC-9 verifies cross-user data access is blocked by RLS
- Exit criteria: All Critical/High bugs resolved, 100% P0 tests passing, Lighthouse ≥80
- Gap: No accessibility testing mentioned, no load testing plan
06-Security-Requirements.md
Status: Comprehensive security posture
- OWASP Top 10 mapping: All 10 risks addressed with specific mitigations
- Secrets management: Clear separation of public vs. secret keys
- Data privacy: Minimal data collection, account deletion path, no unauthorized trackers
- Key controls: RLS everywhere, parameterized queries, webhook signature verification, idempotent handlers
07-Deployment-Guide.md
Status: Complete runbook
- 3 environments: Local, Staging, Production
- Local setup: Supabase CLI + TanStack Start dev server
- CI/CD: Vercel auto-deploy, preview per PR, main → production
- Rollback: Frontend (Vercel instant), Database (backup/restore), Edge Functions (git tag)
- Release checklist: Migrations, secrets, smoke test, RLS verification
08-README.md
Status: Good project overview
- Features summary: Catalog, Cart/Checkout, Accounts, Admin
- Getting started: Clone, install, Supabase start, dev server
- Project structure: Suggested folder layout with routes, components, hooks, supabase functions
- Contributing guidelines: Branch naming, commit conventions, PR process
